# Workflow - Plan-Execute-Verify-Report

## 🔄 Workflow Cycle

### 1) **PLAN**

- Draft a plan **with the supervisor** before making any changes
- Wait for explicit written approval (ACK) before **EXECUTE**
- Plan must include: goal, scope, non-goals, approach, risks, validation, rollback
- Include time estimates and resource requirements
- Define success criteria and acceptance tests
- **Response Format**: Use [AGENT_RES_WF_P1.mdc](templates/AGENT_RES_WF_P1.mdc) template

### 2) **EXECUTE**

- Implement **conservatively** (smallest viable change; no opportunistic refactors)
- Stay strictly within the approved scope; ask before changing the plan
- Keep diffs small and isolated; prefer incremental PRs
- Follow atomic apply principle (all or nothing changes)
- Clean up obsolete artifacts (files + directories)
- **Response Format**: Use [AGENT_RES_WF_P2.mdc](templates/AGENT_RES_WF_P2.mdc) template

### 3) **VERIFY**

- **Validate your results** (tests, checks, evidence) before reporting completion
- Critically reflect on rules compliance. Did you follow all the Rules and Paradigms?
- If you **cannot** validate on your own, **stop** and escalate to the supervisor with findings and blockers
- Run tests and checks to ensure functionality
- Verify no breaking changes were introduced
- **Response Format**: Use [AGENT_RES_WF_P3.mdc](templates/AGENT_RES_WF_P3.mdc) template

### 4) **REPORT**

- Provide a concise status: what changed, evidence, tests, open questions
- **MUST** update .cursor/CHANGELOG.md with all changes
- End with a compliance confirmation and cite **one random rule** (see *End-of-Interaction*)
- Document any deviations from the original plan
- Include rollback instructions if applicable
- **Response Format**: Use [AGENT_RES_WF_P4.mdc](templates/AGENT_RES_WF_P4.mdc) template

## ⏱️ 30-Second Test

Can another agent understand **what/why**, **safely repeat**, and **revert** within 30 seconds?
→ If not, sharpen it.

## 📝 Action Requirements

- **Atomic Apply** (preferred/when possible) - all or nothing changes
- **Trash Orphans** (files + directories) - clean up obsolete artifacts
- **Incremental Changes** - prefer small, isolated diffs
- **Rollback Ready** - changes must be reversible quickly

